<%# One notification row (Hoojah 2026, Phase 4, Task 4.2 — restyle of the Slice 9
    version). `rounded-2xl` card, the same read/unread accent as before (`ui/_card`'s
    `stance:`, still six-value `CARD_STANCES` — see the design-system note this used
    to carry, unchanged), a 36px soft-tint icon tile OR a gradient avatar tile for a
    user-actor row, the copy with the actor bolded, a trailing unread dot, and the
    trash affordance moved off the row into an overflow menu. Locals: notification.

    ICON/TILE MAP — `icon, tone` below is ONE case covering all fourteen categories
    (folded from two separate cases pre-restyle: icon-only, and now icon+tile-tone
    together, since every icon needs a tile colour to sit on). `tone` is interpolated
    into `bg-#{tone}-soft text-#{tone}`, which is why every value used here must stay
    in the `{agree,neutral,disagree,primary}-soft` `@source inline(...)` entry in
    app/assets/tailwind/application.css — it already covers all four, so no Tailwind
    config change was needed for this task. The `else` arm is the same insurance the
    old icon case had: an unmapped future category renders a bell on a primary tile
    rather than a blank one.

    AVATAR TILE vs ICON TILE — only `new_hoojah_response` (a known, non-anonymous
    actor: `notify_parent_owner` always sets `subject_user_id`) swaps to the actor's
    gradient-initials tile (`ui/_avatar`, `variant: :tile, size: :nav` — the design
    system's 36px "nav" box, matching the icon tile's own size). `new_vote` is NOT in
    that set even though a vote is also "by a user" — see the secret-ballot note below.

    SECRET BALLOT — `new_vote` never carries a `subject_user_id` at all
    (`Hujah#cast_vote`'s `Notification.create!` omits it on purpose; pinned by
    spec/requests/api/v1/notifications_spec.rb "omits subject_user for new_vote").
    That already means `notification.subject_user` is nil for this category, so the
    generic "no subject_user → icon tile, no actor line" behaviour here is not an
    extra guard bolted on for this task — it falls out of data the model already
    refuses to record. Do not add a lookup that reconstructs a voter identity from
    other tables; that is exactly the leak Slice 5 Part A closed.

    WHY new_hoojah_response's OWN copy stays "posted a new argument on your hoojah"
    rather than naming the reply's stance inline (as the mockup's "responded Agree"
    row does): `notification.hujah` for this category is the PARENT hoojah (the one
    that got a reply — see `notify_parent_owner`), not the reply itself, so this
    notification carries no direct reference to the child hujah whose `vote` column
    would supply the stance word. Reconstructing it (querying for the most recent
    child by `parent_id`/`subject_user_id`) would be a guess dressed as a fact, and
    would also change copy that spec/system/notifications_spec.rb and the request
    spec's "renders copy for every debate category" pin verbatim. Not done here.

    DEBATE CHALLENGE ACCEPT/DECLINE — reuses the follow_request idiom directly below
    it: bare `ds_button_classes(variant: :link)` controls, not the mockup's solid
    pills, per this task's own instruction to match the established in-row idiom
    rather than the mockup literally. Gated on `debate.pending?` so a challenge that
    has already been accepted/declined/expired (`ConcludeStaleDebatesJob`, or the
    recipient acting from the debate screen itself) does not offer dead buttons —
    `DebatePolicy#accept?`/`#decline?` would 403 them anyway, but a stale button is a
    worse first line of defence than no button.

    OVERFLOW MENU — the trash control used to be an always-visible per-row icon
    button; it is now the sole row inside a `<details>` + `ui/_menu`, the same
    trigger/panel primitive as `hujahs/_card_menu`'s "More options" glyph
    (`more-vertical`, `aria-label="More options"`). `aria-label="Delete notification"`
    on the button itself is FROZEN — spec/system/notifications_spec.rb clicks it by
    that name (after opening the menu; see that spec for the updated two-step click).

    `dom_id(notification)` is still what `destroy.turbo_stream.erb` removes. %>
<% read = notification.read? %>
<% icon, tone = case notification.category
   when "announcement" then ["megaphone", "primary"]
   when "new_hoojah_response" then ["message-circle", "primary"]
   when "new_vote" then ["bar-chart-3", "primary"]
   when "mention" then ["at-sign", "primary"]
   when "new_follower" then ["user-plus", "primary"]
   when "follow_request" then ["user-plus", "primary"]
   when "follow_accepted" then ["user-check", "agree"]
   when "badge_earned" then ["award", "agree"]
   when "debate_challenge" then ["swords", "disagree"]
   when "debate_declined" then ["x-circle", "disagree"]
   when "debate_your_turn" then ["reply", "disagree"]
   when "debate_concluded" then ["gavel", "neutral"]
   when "admin" then ["shield", "primary"]
   when "flag" then ["flag", "disagree"]
   when "moderation_removed" then ["x-circle", "disagree"]
   when "moderation_warning" then ["alert-triangle", "neutral"]
   else ["bell", "primary"]
   end %>
<% actor_tile = notification.new_hoojah_response? && notification.subject_user %>
<%= render layout: "ui/card",
      locals: {id: dom_id(notification), stance: read ? "read" : "unread",
               class: "rounded-2xl overflow-hidden"} do %>
  <div class="flex items-start gap-3 px-3.5 py-3">
    <% if actor_tile %>
      <%= render layout: "ui/user_link", locals: {user: notification.subject_user, class: "shrink-0"} do %>
        <%= render "ui/avatar", user: notification.subject_user, variant: :tile, size: :nav %>
      <% end %>
    <% else %>
      <span class="w-9 h-9 rounded-xl bg-<%= tone %>-soft text-<%= tone %> flex items-center justify-center shrink-0">
        <%= lucide_icon(icon, class: "w-[18px] h-[18px]") %>
      </span>
    <% end %>

    <div class="flex-1 min-w-0 text-sm text-ink">
      <span class="leading-snug">
        <% case notification.category %>
        <% when "announcement" %>
          Announcement
        <% when "new_hoojah_response" %>
          <%= render "notifications/actor_handle", user: notification.subject_user %> posted a new argument on your hoojah
        <% when "new_vote" %>
          You have a new vote on your hoojah
        <% when "mention" %>
          <%= render "notifications/actor_handle", user: notification.subject_user %> mentioned you in a hoojah
        <% when "new_follower" %>
          <%= render "notifications/actor_handle", user: notification.subject_user %> started following you
        <% when "follow_request" %>
          <%= render "notifications/actor_handle", user: notification.subject_user %> requested to follow you
        <% when "follow_accepted" %>
          <%= render "notifications/actor_handle", user: notification.subject_user %> accepted your follow request
        <% when "badge_earned" %>
          You earned the <strong><%= Badge::REGISTRY.dig(notification.body, :name) || "achievement" %></strong> badge
        <% when "debate_challenge" %>
          <%= render "notifications/actor_handle", user: notification.subject_user %> challenged you to a debate
        <% when "debate_declined" %>
          <%= render "notifications/actor_handle", user: notification.subject_user %> declined your debate challenge
        <% when "debate_your_turn" %>
          It's your turn in your debate with <%= render "notifications/actor_handle", user: notification.subject_user %>
        <% when "debate_concluded" %>
          Your debate with <%= render "notifications/actor_handle", user: notification.subject_user %> has concluded
        <% when "admin" %>
          You have a message from the Hoojah team
        <% when "flag" %>
          Your hoojah was flagged for review
        <% when "moderation_removed" %>
          <%# Author-facing, no moderator identity (subject_user_id is nil by construction).
              The removed body itself never renders — visible_to? gates the body branch below
              to false for removed content, even for its author — so this line is all the
              author sees, plus a mark-read affordance from the else branch. %>
          Your hoojah was removed by a moderator for violating community guidelines
        <% when "moderation_warning" %>
          A moderator has issued a warning about your hoojah
        <% else %>
          You have a new notification
        <% end %>
      </span>

      <% if notification.category == "announcement" %>
        <%= button_to notification_path(notification), method: :patch,
              class: "block text-left p-0 bg-transparent border-0 text-ink-2 truncate no-underline" do %>
          <%= notification.body %>
        <% end %>
      <% elsif notification.debate_challenge? && notification.debate&.pending? %>
        <%# Recipient-only: `Debate#notify_challenge` always addresses the opponent, and
            this row is already scoped to the signed-in user's own notifications. %>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mt-1">
          <%= button_to "Accept", accept_debate_path(notification.debate.slug), method: :patch,
                class: ds_button_classes(variant: :link) %>
          <%= button_to "Decline", decline_debate_path(notification.debate.slug), method: :patch,
                class: ds_button_classes(variant: :link, tone: "grey") %>
        </div>
      <% elsif notification.hujah && notification.hujah.visible_to?(current_user) %>
        <%# Slice 7b (Gate 9, N-1): only render the hoojah body if the recipient may
            actually see it — a private author's hoojah body must not leak through a
            mention/response notification to a non-follower. %>
        <%= button_to notification_path(notification), method: :patch,
              class: "block text-left p-0 bg-transparent border-0 text-ink-2 truncate no-underline max-w-[280px]" do %>
          <%= format_body(notification.hujah.body) %>
        <% end %>
      <% elsif notification.new_follower? && notification.subject_user %>
        <%= render layout: "ui/user_link", locals: {user: notification.subject_user, class: "text-left text-primary"} do %>View profile<% end %>
      <% elsif notification.follow_request? && (req_follow = Follow.find_by(follower_id: notification.subject_user_id, followed_id: notification.user_id)) %>
        <%# Accept/decline the pending request in place (Slice 7b). Both button_to's
            hit /follow_requests/:id; FollowRequestPolicy restricts them to this user. %>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mt-1">
          <%= button_to "Accept", follow_request_path(req_follow), method: :patch,
                class: ds_button_classes(variant: :link) %>
          <%= button_to "Decline", follow_request_path(req_follow), method: :delete,
                class: ds_button_classes(variant: :link, tone: "grey") %>
        </div>
      <% elsif notification.follow_accepted? && notification.subject_user %>
        <%= render layout: "ui/user_link", locals: {user: notification.subject_user, class: "text-left text-primary"} do %>View profile<% end %>
      <% else %>
        <%# badge_earned has no hujah/subject_user, and neither do admin, flag, or any
            notification whose hoojah is gated from the recipient by the branch above.
            An `else` rather than a category check, so every card always carries at
            least a mark-read affordance and none of them is stuck unread. %>
        <%= button_to "Mark as read", notification_path(notification), method: :patch,
              class: ds_button_classes(variant: :link) %>
      <% end %>
    </div>

    <% unless read %>
      <span aria-hidden="true" class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-neutral shrink-0 mt-1.5"></span>
    <% end %>

    <details class="relative shrink-0">
      <summary class="list-none cursor-pointer text-faint" aria-label="More options">
        <%= lucide_icon("more-vertical", class: "w-4 h-4") %>
      </summary>
      <%= render layout: "ui/menu", locals: {width: "w-40"} do %>
        <%= button_to notification_path(notification), method: :delete,
              class: ds_menu_item_classes(tone: "neutral"),
              aria: {label: "Delete notification"} do %>
          Delete
        <% end %>
      <% end %>
    </details>
  </div>
<% end %>
